Let DIARIZATION_MODEL pick the pyannote checkpoint at runtime.

Upstream (learnedmachine/whisperx-asr-service) hardcodes
pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1. We want to A/B it against
speaker-diarization-3.1 without editing Python source inside a running
container. See HANDOFF-speaker-diarization.md section 3.2.

Previously this was applied with `docker cp`, which silently reverted on
`--force-recreate` / image rebuild. It is now baked into the image by
docker/asr-service/Dockerfile.

If this patch stops applying, the base image changed its diarization
loader. Regenerate against the new base (see docker/asr-service/README.md)
instead of deleting the check.

--- a/app/pipeline.py
+++ b/app/pipeline.py
@@ -754,9 +754,18 @@
     if _diarize_pipeline is None:
         with _model_load_lock:
             if _diarize_pipeline is None:
-                logger.info("Loading diarization pipeline: pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1")
+                # DIARIZATION_MODEL lets operators swap in a different pyannote
+                # checkpoint without editing code. Both of these work with the
+                # same HF token:
+                #   pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1  (default, newer)
+                #   pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1          (older, well-tested)
+                diarize_model = (
+                    os.getenv("DIARIZATION_MODEL", "").strip()
+                    or "pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1"
+                )
+                logger.info(f"Loading diarization pipeline: {diarize_model}")
                 pipeline = DiarizationPipeline(
-                    model_name="pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1",
+                    model_name=diarize_model,
                     use_auth_token=HF_TOKEN,
                     device=torch.device(DEVICE),
                 )
